<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim Nagwamatse</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim Nagwamatse was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kontagora">Kontagora</a> from 1880, son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>'s founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umaru-nagwamatse">Umaru Nagwamatse</a>. Under him the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slave-raiding">slave raiding</a> on which Kontagora lived reached its peak, depopulating much of the region. British forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Frederick Lugard</a> attacked Kontagora in 1901, and he was captured in 1902.</p></div>
